{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/695940-hey-i-need-a-favor","id":695940,"title":"\"Hey, I need a favor\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-10T05:06:44-07:00","id":695940,"title":"\"Hey, I need a favor\"","content":"I have a concept in my head largely based on my own personality flaws, that of being an incorrigible mooch. The idea is a guy who's nice, fun, charming, and a complete mess, going about everything with an endearing awkwardness that trips people's protective instincts. He instantly becomes your best friend.<br /> <br /> Then he says the title: &quot;Hey, I need a favor.&quot;<br /> <br /> Whether it's borrowing something he has no intent to return, getting you to do some chore for him becaus he's &quot;too busy&quot; or treating you like an unpaid Uber drive, he smiles, apologizes, and takes a part of your life. The favors escalate, what started as a friendship now fills you with dread, and (as he starts to use atavisms more blatantly) you find it utterly impossible to do anything but agree once he's standing in front of you, no matter how much righteous indignation you've stocked up.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hey, I need a favor.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm not sure which splats to go with, but Makara Collector makes the most sense to me. He's more about the metaphorical sense of drowning in his endless need, and he is a thief of time, thus your very life. Problem is that I think he might be too abstract on both counts, but can't think of anything that'd fit better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8404-luckystampede","name":"LuckyStampede","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T06:28:45-07:00","id":696006,"title":"","content":"Makara is a really nice choice. Especially when from &quot;hey, may you pass me your notes&quot; (s)he starts asking &quot;erm... i'm not so sure i'll pass this exam, would you mind helping me to cheat?&quot; to &quot;sorry, the teacher was really enraged agains me... and... now... well... do you have a bath-tub? I just bought the acid, just before coming here.&quot; <br /> <br /> Maybe Tyrant is a more appropriate choice - after all, what (s)he thrives on is the power to make people do things for her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1304-baroqo","name":"Baroqo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T10:16:20-07:00","id":696230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baroqo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/695940-hey-i-need-a-favor?p=696006#post696006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Makara is a really nice choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I feel that the secondary aspects of each family, or how they manifest in different forms in the modern day, were discussed more. Like, how Makara are also the fear of infinity, something as applicable to the vacuum of space to the briny deeps, and how you can metaphorically drown in many things, be it smothering affection or endless grasping <i>need.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baroqo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/695940-hey-i-need-a-favor?p=696006#post696006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe Tyrant is a more appropriate choice - after all, what (s)he thrives on is the power to make people do things for her.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, considering I'm using this to work out some personality issues, I think it's telling that that prospect did not even occur to me. Until this moment, I never considered passive-aggressive mooching as a form of domination/control, and now it seems really obvious.<br /> <br /> Making the character female also seems like a good idea, because that's one extra step removed from myself (and I play female characters pretty well). I'll have to see though, it's a bit harder if I'm playing in person than online, and still looking for a group.<br /> <br /> I picture my character's Soul as this vast, grasping knot of tentacles. Tentacles everywhere. Tentacles all the way down. In fact, there doesn't even seem to be a body at the core of all the tentacles, just a thicker knot, like a koosh ball made of tentacles instead of plastic strings...that description kinda undercuts the horror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8404-luckystampede","name":"LuckyStampede","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T13:55:41-07:00","id":696466,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna be honest Tyrant makes more sense to me than Collector. I mean with a Collector having something is the important aspect, so the escalation would be having more and more people in this sort of relationship with it. Whereas a Tyrant the escalation you've listed could work as while you're only dealing with one or a few people being able to push them to ever greater inconveniences despite them not wanting fits it more effectively.<br /> <br /> Another angle you might want to look at is the Ugallu. Like you said the whole drowning fits for the Makara, The Ugallu for another angel also includes mention of dragging things out for the fall and stripping away protections and such one piece at a time and the initial section actually includes a mention of the victim dreading or being in fear of the Ugallu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T05:35:29-07:00","id":696956,"title":"","content":"The Ugallu to me have a sense of suddenness: while a hunt may be careful and gradual to them, to the target it comes out of nowhere. So for the OP's idea, I'm more inclined to throw my vote behind Makara - they're better for the sense of it getting worse and worse. Also I agree with making it a Tyrant rather than a Collector.<br /> <br /> Btw, one of the things I like about Beast is its potential for lacing monstrosity and supernature into very ordinary interactions; in that light, this is a really good character idea.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T07:08:52-07:00","id":697064,"title":"","content":"I'mma Gonna Throw out an Odd idea, Namtaru as the Family, Tryant/Predator for the Hunger, the &quot;Repulsion&quot; (s)he Embodies is &quot;Self&quot; or the Question &quot;Would I not want someone else to help me if i needed it?&quot; feeding on someones Self confindance is likely to be abit Dark in my Eyes though but, the idea is out there now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T15:28:33-07:00","id":701340,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I was about to suggest Namtaru also, since they're about making people feel something when they're around you. Although for the Hunger, I would like to propose they hunger for ruin.<br /> <br /> <br /> Why a Gorgon Ravager? You said they're very charismatic and others can't help but go along with them. Well, how many times have we heard the story of impressionable men and women getting swept up in someone's charismatic demeanor, only to be lead down a self destructive path with a tragic end? The favors seem harmless at first and they seem like a cool guy / girl as they build up the friendship, but eventually the favors turn worse and the victim goes along with it out of a sense of loyalty or the belief it's a one time thing. But it's not a one time thing, it keeps happening and ever since the first time, you're in too deep, you're an accomplice to gods only know what!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Don't worry about being too obscure with a character though, especially regarding a Beast. Dreams and nightmares often display themselves in metaphors and symbolism. For example, did you know that spiders are supposed to represent you avoiding your problems in life? There's any number of forms a Beast's soul can manifest itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-14-2015, 06:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}